}^{-4x}.\n$$" 13194139535356 true] [17592186345583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345584 13194139535356 true] [17592186345583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345585 13194139535356 true] [17592186345583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345586 13194139535356 true] [17592186345583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345587 13194139535356 true] [17592186345583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345588 13194139535356 true] [17592186345583 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535356 true] [17592186345583 1041 "selection" 13194139535356 true] [17592186345583 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345584 13194139535356 true] [17592186345583 1110 #uuid "837fcb19-470e-5255-b32e-1b6facaab254" 13194139535356 true] [17592186345584 1034 "y=A{e}^{-4x}+Bx{e}^{-4x}" 13194139535356 true] [17592186345584 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535356 true] [17592186345584 1111 #uuid "f6e48b0e-ea41-5e8f-8528-8e942eaff8f3" 13194139535356 true] [17592186345585 1034 "y=A{e}^{-4x}+Bx{e}^{-2x}" 13194139535356 true] [17592186345585 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535356 true] [17592186345585 1111 #uuid "4093dd62-d060-513b-93cb-2cd3ba433998" 13194139535356 true] [17592186345586 1034 "y=A{e}^{-4x}+Bx{e}^{2x}" 13194139535356 true] [17592186345586 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535356 true] [17592186345586 1111 #uuid "8fa7010b-730e-5b92-ac41-e26d6c027f3b" 13194139535356 true] [17592186345587 1034 "y=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{8x}" 13194139535356 true] [17592186345587 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535356 true] [17592186345587 1111 #uuid "c7c04272-4291-555e-83ee-643104567280" 13194139535356 true] [17592186345588 1034 "y=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{4x}" 13194139535356 true] [17592186345588 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535356 true] [17592186345588 1111 #uuid "a849d5bc-8950-582d-85e3-091352e7f9b3" 13194139535356 true] [17592186345589 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345590 13194139535356 true] [17592186345589 1089 "q-79934" 13194139535356 true] [17592186345589 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535356 true] [17592186345589 1100 "Given that ${y}_{1}(t)={t}^{2}$ is a solution to the equation ${t}^{2}{y}^{″}-2t{y}^{′}+2y=0$ for $t>0,$ use reduction of order to find a second solution ${y}_{2}(t)$ to the equation, and write down the general solution." 13194139535356 true] [17592186345589 1113 #uuid "25b6d0d4-7825-556a-b87b-d3677af04db8" 13194139535356 true] [17592186345589 1145 "According to the reduction of order method, we let ${y}_{2}=u(t){t}^{2}.$\n\nDifferentiating the above with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′} & ={u}^{′}{t}^{2}+2ut \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″} & ={u}^{″}{t}^{2}+4{u}^{′}t+2u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}({u}^{″}{t}^{2}+4{u}^{′}t+2u)-2t({u}^{′}{t}^{2}+2ut)+2(u{t}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ {u}^{″}{t}^{4}+4{u}^{′}{t}^{3}+2u{t}^{2}-2{u}^{′}{t}^{3}-4u{t}^{2}+2u{t}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {u}^{″}{t}^{4}+2{u}^{′}{t}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}^{3}(t{u}^{″}+2{u}^{′}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${t}^{3}\\ne 0$ for $t>0,$ we must have\n\n$$\nt{u}^{″}+2{u}^{′}=0.\n$$\n\nLet $w={u}^{′}.$ Then our equation becomes\n\n$$\nt{w}^{′}+2w=0.\n$$\n\nThis is a separable equation that has the solution\n\n$$\nw=\\frac{{c}_{1}}{{t}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nBut since $w={u}^{′},$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}=\\frac{{c}_{1}}{{t}^{2}}\\,⟹\\,u=-\\frac{{c}_{1}}{t}+{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our expression for ${y}_{2}(t)=u{t}^{2}$ becomes\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(t)=(-\\frac{{c}_{1}}{t}+{c}_{2}){t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSetting ${c}_{1}=-1$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(t)=t.\n$$\n\nFinally, because $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})=-{t}^{2}\\ne 0,$ we know that ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are independent (you should verify this calculation yourself).\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A{t}^{2}+Bt.\n$$" 13194139535356 true] [17592186345590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345591 13194139535356 true] [17592186345590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345592 13194139535356 true] [17592186345590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345593 13194139535356 true] [17592186345590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345594 13194139535356 true] [17592186345590 1000 #edb/ref 17592